label act1_day11:

    scene bg black
    "Friday"
    
    scene bg school_main_hall
    "Today has been quite the experience due to everyone preparing for the festival. "

    "Either a class is nearly dead due to most of the students working on their events or we get pulled into helping out. I've probably helped at least 3 displays already due to classmates scrambling for last minute help."

    "It doesn't help that the teachers are basically treating today as a day off at work."

    "As I head through the halls with my lunch I start to contemplate a good location. There's a lot of people working throughout the cafeteria today and I'd rather not be dragged into more free labor."

    "As I stand in the hallway, my mental wandering is pleasantly interrupted."

    m "For someone so down to earth, you sure do like to keep your head in the clouds, huh?"

    mc "Oh! Hey Monika. I was just trying to figure out where to eat. "

    mc "The current winning option is back in the classroom. Can't be late if I'm already there."

    m "Quite the efficient decision. I was just about to head up-"

    "Just then I grab Monika by the shoulders and pull her to the side, just before a pair of students carrying an elaborate set piece almost run into her. "

    "The two guys carrying it look back at us and realized how close they cut the corner."

    st "Scuse me! Sorry bout that!"

    mc "Just be careful there, buddy."
    "I turn to Monika, who looks to be in shock."

    mc "You okay?"

    "Monika looks down to the floor as she answers."

    m "Uhh huh.."

    "Her face slowly goes from pale to red as I realize I'm still holding her."

    mc "S-sorry. Didn't mean to throw you around like that."

    m "It's alright. You did save me after all."

    "As she looks up to me, I can't help but think of how this looks. "

    "I release her shoulders and pick my lunchbox off the floor."

    m "Umm, as I was saying, I was about to head up to the roof to eat. Would you like to join me?"

    mc "Eh, I don't know. I don't want to be the weird guy in your friend group."

    m "Well first off, too late."

    mc "ha ha. I see Natsuki's gotten to you too."

    m "Heehee, I couldn't resist. But I was actually going alone. Get a bit of a break from the crowds."

    "I raise an eyebrow out of confusion."

    mc "Uhh, wouldn't inviting me ruin your alone time?"
    m "I just needed a break from crowds, not from company. You know what they say, two's a company..."

    "I begin to offer a rebuttal, but I blank out on any reason why I shouldn't join her."

    mc "Okay, sure. I'll be happy to join you."

    m "Wonderful! Let's go before anything else comes flying out at us."

    "As Monika leads the way, I shortly follow."

    scene bg school_stairs
    "As we're walking towards the roof together, the stares and whispers in the crowds are starting to creep in."

    qu "Do you see who she's with?"

    qu "Lucky bastard."

    qu "Wonder how long they've been at it."

    "This isn't good. Should I..say something? "

    "As I look at Monika, it doesn't look like it's phasing her. Maybe she can't hear it? "

    "But with her status, she probably hears it all the time. That's probably it. "

    "I can see her brushing off the comments from others effortlessly."

    st "Talk about a slam dunk rebound."

    "I stop in my tracks."

    " I..I can't. "
    "I doubt she cares, but I don't want others seeing her like that. I especially don't want this getting back to-"

    m "Hey, you okay?"

    "I look back at her and I can see the concern on her face. "

    "Now that I think about it, she cares so much for us all, she doesn't need to worry about these fruitless rumors anyway. If they don't bother her, they shouldn't bother me."

    mc "Yeah. I'm fine. Just got lost in thought again."

    m "Yeah, it's kinda noisy in here. Good thing we'll be away from all that shortly."

    mc "Yeah."

    "So she did notice. I can see it on her face, but I can tell she doesn't want it to show. "

    "Just ignore them like she is. I mean, it could be worse. A rumor like us going out isn't too bad if I think about it..."

    scene bg roof_1

    "As the door opens to the roof, the sunlight is nearly blinding. "

    "As my eyes adjust, I can take in just how peaceful it is up here. There's quite a view as well as the neighborhood is shorter in stature than the school, giving quite a line of sight. "

    "The lack of others is also surreal from my reality of school life."

    mc "Wow, it's so..quiet here. Kinda surprised that more people don't take advantage of it."

    m "Well if they did, that would defeat the purpose of us being here, wouldn't it?"

    "I nod my head in agreement until I fall onto the implications. "

    "As I watch Monika sit down on the inner ledge, she pats on the area next to her. "

    "I sheepishly walk over and sit down, being EXTREMELY conscious of where I sit. Not too far, but not to close."

    "I place my food on my lap and begin to uncover it. I really can't thank Sayori's mom enough for those recipes. I didn't think pan seared chicken breast and roasted potatoes and onions were so easy. "

    "I take a glance at what Monika brought. "

    "It's a neat salad with a variety of vegetables, some fresh cut fruit, and what looks to be some sort of meat square?"

    mc "Hey, what kinda meat is that?"

    m "Oh, this is actually tofu. They're quite good when seasoned and roasted like this."

    mc "Really? I've never tried tofu before."

    "Monika peers up at me as she cuts her tofu. She then places it in my container. "

    "I look back and she silently smiles to herself while taking a bite. I pick it up and take a bite. "

    "Oh, wow! I thought it would taste like some slimy gel, but the seasonings in this seem to seep through the entire thing and are fully bursting with flavor."

    mc "Mmm..that's better than I was expecting. I might need to try this at home."

    m "I made it myself, so I can send you the recipe, if you want."

    mc "Definitely!"

    "I start cutting into my chicken and begin to portion it. As I take a bite, a sense of familiarity with the taste hits me."

    mc "Hmmm. That's crazy."

    m "Hmm? Is something wrong with your food?"

    mc "Quite the opposite. I think I used some of the same seasonings on my chicken that you did with the tofu. Their flavor isn't one to one, but quite close."

    m "I guess we have the same tastes in seasonings."

    mc "Here. Try a bit and tell me what you think."

    "I use my knife as a skewer and hold the piece of chicken towards her."

    m "It's sweet to offer, but I'll pass."

    mc "...Oh. Okay."

    m "And it's not that I think it's not good. It's just that I'm a vegetarian."

    mc "Oh...looking at your lunch, that makes sense. So is it some diet you're on or something?"

    m "Not really. I just choose to be vegetarian. After learning of the process of meat production, I literally couldn't stomach it anymore."

    mc "Oh, sorry. I guess I shouldn't have-"

    m "No no no! I'm not mad or upset at all. Maybe a few years ago I would have been. "

    m "I was...huh...quite insufferable starting out. But, over time, I understood more about other's outlooks and accepted others eating meat. "

    m "I just chose not to take part in it anymore. I'm sure that probably makes me sound pretentious, doesn't it."

    mc "Not at all. If anything, it makes you sound understanding, yet firm to your convictions. Sounds cool to me."

    "Monika stares blankly in shock. After a while she starts to smile lightly."

    m "You know, potatoes and onions are vegetarian. And yours smell quite good."

    "I hold my container over to her, making sure the side not touching the chicken was closest to her."

    mc "Feel free to help yourself."

    "Monika gingerly picks up a decent sized potato and a ring of onion."

    "As she bites into it, her eyes widen."

    m "[player]! This is delicious!"

    mc "Ah, it's nothing."

    m "Let's see, poet, chef, are there any other talents you're hiding from me?"

    "I begin to blush from the compliments as I turn my head to look away from Monika. "

    "It's so rare to hear praise outside of just following general directions. "

    "This support feels...nice."

    mc "Heck, I'm just following a recipe. I got quite a few from Sayori's mom a while back. "
    mc "I can look through them for some vegetarian options, or even ones where the meat can be left out."

    "As I turn back to her with the offer, I see a slight disappointment on her face, but it's quickly replaced with her somber smile."

    m "That would be good. Thank you."

    "We then continue to eat our food in silence."

    "..."

    "Should I...say something? I noticed that she looked a bit down for a second, but..."

    "As I look at her I can't help but be a bit mesmerized by her beauty. Even the way she chews is adorable."

    "No! stop. Don't start staring again. She's a friend. A cute friend, but..."

    "NO! None of that! This is your club president! She is just doing this to be nice and to get to know me better as a club member. "

    "She's probably done this with the others as well. Just because it's a guy and a girl alone, doesn't mean anything will-"

    m "So, are you feeling ready for the festival?"

    mc "AHH-  *COUGH COUGH COUGH*"

    "My impromptu choking fit slightly spooks Monika. As she reaches to pat me on the back, "

    " As she reaches to pat me on the back, I grab my drink and take a quick guzzle, clearing the food from my throat."

    m "Oh my God, are you okay?!"

    mc "Yea, just..food went down before I was done chewing. I'm good now."

    m "That's a relief . You scared me there."

    mc "Yeah, death by chicken is not a good way to go. I guess I should probably consider vegetarianism as well."

    m "Well, that is an advantage. I hope that wasn't your response to my question, though."

    mc "To be honest, I really don't know how I'll perform. I've never really done anything public like that, so my nerves are kinda shaking at the thought."

    "I turn to Monika and can see a bit of disappointment on her face."

    mc "That's not to say I'm gonna back out of it. I'll give it a try. Just...don't hold too much hope for me. Best leave your expectations low."

    m "No."

    mc "Wha-"

    m "No. I will not lower my expectations of you. "

    m "You have talent. You are capable of so much more than you give yourself credit for."

    mc "But...uh...I-"

    "Monika grabs my hand as she turns towards me and looks me in the eyes with a stern look on her face."

    m "I get how you feel, [player]. Despite my reputation, I can get quite nervous myself. But if I let those feelings take over, I would just let others down. "

    m "So that's why I always do my best no matter what."

    "I stare blankly back, unable to respond. "

    "What can I even say at this point?"

    m "I wouldn't ask you this if I didn't have faith in you. "

    m "And I've noticed how much this club has helped you. I just want to try and help others in the same way. "

    m "Showing your growth in such a short period of time to others will be a great help for any students considering joining the club as a whole, and..well...me..."

    "She slowly lets go of my hand and looks away."

    m "S-sorry. I got a little-"

    "I grab her hand back as if I'm giving her a handshake."

    mc "You're right. With all the club has done for me, it would be selfish not to give it my all. You have my word."

    "Monika's face lights up."

    m "Thank you, [player]. I have no doubt that your performance will have an impact."

    "Whether that impact is positive or not remains to be seen, but I'll keep that bit of pessimism to myself for now."

    mc "So, what if we don't get any new members out of this?"

    "Monika begins to side eye me with a bit of contempt in her eye."
    mc "N-not to say that it won't happen! If anything we may get too many members! "
    mc "Just, hypothetically. Did you have, like, any target number?"

    m "Honestly, I would like our numbers to double with underclassmen. "

    m "I mean, a newly formed club made of only seniors seems so one and done, and I want better for the literature club."

    mc "Ahh. Passing it on to others. I can see that. "

    mc "But, I don't see anything wrong with what we have now. "

    mc "Sure, that means once we graduate it's over, but that's in name only. "

    mc "The experiences we share will stay with us long after the fact."

    m "Yeah. It's quite the bittersweet consolation."

    "Monika sits and stares at the few bites left of her food. Her stone face slowly warms as a smile curls."

    m "As long as we have fun and give it our all, the results don't matter. Even if no one joins, we still fall nothing less than perfect in my eyes."

    "Yeah. While it was a bit rocky at first, the chemistry in the club is really comfortable as is. New members or not, we still have something special here."

    mc "Monika?"

    m "Hmm?"

    mc "Thank you. For everything you've done. "

    mc "For forming this club, inviting me, supporting us all, and pushing us to become our best selves. I know you know about..."
    "My lips begin to quiver a bit. Even trying to say her name is doing this still?"

    m "It's okay. I know it's still a sore spot despite the growth you've shown. That's expected. Healing takes time. "

    m "I am here to support you as much as I can. It's what friends do."

    "I can feel my eyes getting watery from her words. I blink them away as I wipe my eyes."

    mc "I'm glad to have a friend as caring as you, Monika. Thank you."

    "Monika begins to blush and look away smiling."

    m "I'm glad to have a friend who returns that kindness. I can't tell you how rare that is."

    "We finish our lunch just as the warning bell goes off. We both pack our stuff and head to the door."

    m "Thank you for joining me, [player]. Your company was a refreshing change of pace for me."

    mc "Same. And thanks for the invite. It's nice to spend time outside of club."

    m "We should do it again sometime."


    mc "You bet."

    "As we walk back into the school and part ways, I look back on Monika walking the other way. "

    "As I do, our eyes meet as she is doing the same. "

    "While I expected her to look away like I've noticed before, this time she smiles at me with a crimson glow on her face waving. I wave back as I turn the corner and head to class."

    scene bg club_day
    "As I walk through the door of the clubroom, I anticipate the same sight I've grown accustomed to..."

    "Wait..."

    "No one else is here."

    "I back out and take a look at the room number. "

    "Yup. Right room. "

    "I take a look at my phone just in case I missed a message that the club was canceled. Nope. No messages in the group chat. "

    "Huh. I must be the first one here. Weird."

    "I take a seat close to where Sayori usually sits and pull out my poems. I gotta make a decision today about which one I'll perform. "

    "I think back about how I was feeling while writing all three. "

    "While I feel my latest has the best message and is generally more positive, I can't overlook the emotions I poured into my second one."

    #"[Flashback to this scene and line]"
    "***Monika: You are capable of so much more than you give yourself credit for.***"

    "Those words echo in my head. If I can perform with the emotion I had when writing this, I know I can make Monika proud."

    "As I read over my poem to rehearse, I hear the door open and see Yuri walking in."

    y "Oh. Hello, [player]. I'm quite surprised to find you here so early."

    "[player]; Yeah. It was a bit weird coming to an empty room. I was just going over my poems to make a decision on which one to choose to perform. "

    mc "How are you feeling about the festival?"

    y "Uuuuu..."

    "As to be expected from Yuri."

    y "I still have my reservations, but I will see the performance through. "

    y "I hope. "

    y "Possibly."

    "She begins to slump as she seems to be simulating the situation in her head. I then notice that her hands seem to be shaking. I get up and walk briskly over to her."

    mc "Woah there, Yuri. It's okay. Do you need to sit down?"

    "As she looks up at me, her eyes are glossy from tears."

    y "I don't think I can do this, but I can't not, and..I can't...I just..."

    "As she's starting to hyperventilate. "

    "I grab her hand, which feels icy cold. It seemed to startle her a bit, but she squeezes my hand back and begins to slow down her breathing."

    mc "Hey, it's okay to feel like this. Believe me, I'm worried too."

    y "I just don't- *exhale* I do not want to be the failing factor in our performance. If I do not perform properly, I will be letting all of you down."

    mc "Yuri. You know that isn't true. I know you've got this. We all do."

    "Yuri slowly looks up at me. Her eyes are completely red. "

    "She fumbles around in her bag and grabs a tissue out of a small pack that she has and begins wiping her eyes."

    y "I have been practicing relentlessly in my room and I am feeling more comfortable with reciting my poem. It's just.. When I think of the crowd...the unfamiliar faces...staring...judging..."

    "Her grip on my hand grows tighter. "

    "This is bad. I'm starting to believe she can't do it either. "

    "Until I remember what Monika said to me."

    mc "You are capable of so much more than you give yourself credit for."

    y "I...I know what I can and can't do. I can't keep my mind still from the eyes on me. I know I will freeze up."

    mc "So it's the crowds that make you uneasy?"

    "Yuri nods."

    mc "Okay, let's forget about the crowd. Let's just focus on the poem. How is that going?"

    y "I have pretty much committed it to memory in its entirety. I went over it dozens of times last night for refinement of the language and optimized it for verbal performance. "

    y "There were a few points where the cadence could be refined."

    mc "That's great! Do you think you can recite it now?"

    "Yuri nods. She then begins softly reciting her poem. "

    "I pick up on one or two small differences, but other than that, it sounds the same as yesterday."

    mc "Sounds like you've got that down pact. I've got no question you won't do great."

    y "I know you are just saying that due to this situation."

    mc "I mean, yeah. But that doesn't make it any less true. "

    mc "If the only thing holding you back is the people, then just forget about them."

    y "How do you expect me to forget that there are dozens of my peers staring at me imparting judgement on my performance?"

    mc "Pretend you are in your room and use your poem written out. I've noticed how you can ignore the world and dive into your books. "

    mc "I've experienced that invisibility first hand, remember."

    y "Hmm hmm...I do apologize."


    mc "No need to, we can use that as a strength. "

    mc "If you're up there and are feeling nervous, just start reading. Reading your own work. "

    mc "Let your own pages pull you into the emotions and that will carry through to your performance."

    y "But I have already memorized it. What would be the point of reading it?"

    mc "The crowd doesn't know you memorized it. Use that to your advantage. You have something to look at that aren't other people so you can lose yourself in the poem."

    "Yuri's grip begins to relax from my hand as color starts to fade back into her face."

    y "I appreciate your suggestion and will definitely be using it. Thank you, [player]."

    "As I let go of her hand and back away, she finishes wiping her eyes and stares into her bag for a moment."

    y "Umm...Excuse me. I just realized I forgot something. I will return shortly."

    mc "Yeah, okay."

    "Yuri briskly walks out of the room, which is soon occupied by an aggressively concerned Natsuki. "

    "As soon as she notices me, she approaches my desk and slams her palms on the desk."
    n "What did you do to Yuri?"

    mc "W-what? I was just helping her-"

    n "How is making her cry helping her? Her face was red and puffy and she didn't even see me when I walked right past her."

    mc "I was talking to her about the festival and-"

    n "Dude. How dense are you? Why would you even bring that up?"

    mc "I was just making conversation! I was going over my poems and so I-"

    n "Don't give me that. You must have done something more to make her cry so hard she can't even be in the same room as you."

    mc "I swear, I didn't do anything. I think she might have forgotten something in a class?"

    n "Fine. I'll ask her when she gets back. If you did anything to her, I will make sure this is an all girls club."

    mc " I swear I didn't do anything and I don't think you have the authority to kick me out of the club."

    n "Who said anything about kicking you out?"

    "Gulp. Please hurry back, Yuri."

    "Natsuki looks around the club"

    n "Don't tell me you scared Monika and Sayori off as well."

    mc "Why do you think I'm scaring everyone off? What am I doing in that brain of yours that would scare them all away?"

    n "I dunno. Probably whatever you were trying with Monika on the roof."

    mc "...You mean eating?"

    n "Sick! I knew YOU were a perv, but I thought Monika had more class than to do that at school."

    mc "..."

    "My face gets red hot from the embarrassment and anger after understanding what she meant."

    mc "LUNCH! WE WERE BOTH JUST EATING LUNCH!!"

    n "What's that? You said munch?"

    mc "Hrrmmm! I just can't with you right now!"

    s "Hey! What's with all the yelling in here? I heard it from down the hall."

    "Sayori walks through the door and approaches us."

    n "I'm just interrogating [player] since he's become a sexual deviant and scared off Yuri."

    mc "I HAVE NOT AND I DID NOT!"

    n "He was probably trying to get her to do some rooftop antics"

    mc "Natsukiiii!!!"

    "I get up and start chasing her while she trots behind Sayori giggling her head off."

    s "[player]? What's going on?"

    mc "Nothing. Natsuki's just being an ass."

    s "So what DID happen to Yuri. And what is a 'rooftop antic'?"

    mc "She-"

    "As soon as I open my mouth the door opens and Yuri walks in. "

    "We all stare at her and she stares back with a confused look on her face."

    y "Was there something that I missed?"

    "Natsuki runs over to Yuri and turns her away from me and Sayori."

    n "Yuri. You're safe with friends now. Now tell me, what did [player] do to you? Did he touch you?"

    mc "What!?"

    n "Sayori! Put a muzzle on him!"

    mc "What are you- mmmrm hrmmm mammal!"

    "My question was interrupted by Sayori's hand clasping tight over my mouth."

    n "Yuri. It's okay. You're safe. Did he touch you?"

    y "Uhh...yes?"

    "Everyone's eyes open wide in surprise. I am soon pelted with slaps from Sayori." #slap sound effects

    s "[player]! How could you?!"

    mc "What the hell, Yuri?"

    y "Wait, what is going on?"

    n "The little perv is getting what he deserves for touching you like that."

    y "I do not. OH NO! Sayori! Stop!"

    "Sayori freezes with her hand in mid air."

    y "There seems to be some miscommunication. When I stated he touched me, it was not in an inappropriate manner. He was just holding my hand for comfort."

    y "He was providing emotional support because I...uh...had a moment of weakness. "

    y "He was kind enough to provide assistance. I assure you he did not attempt anything lewd in nature."

    mc "See? I'm innocent!"

    "Monika walks in and sees me shielding myself from Sayori as she still has her hand floating in a hitting position."

    m "...Do I want to know?"


    n "Only if you're okay with not knowing about the crap your boyfriend is doing to Yuri."

    m "My boyfriend? What are you-"

    m "...Oh. Oh God."

    "Monika places her face in her palm as she mumbles to herself."

    m "As if I didn't hear enough of this in class..."

    m "Yuri? What happened?"

    n "She didn't deny it..."

    y "I think Natsuki is terrorizing [player] by intentionally taking situations out of context and proportion."

    n "I'm just doing my civic duty and making sure he doesn't step out of line."

    m "Thank you for your service, but it shouldn't be at the expense of [player]'s integrity."

    n "I mean, I doubt there's any there, but then again, he probably showed you his integrity on the roof, so I'll take your word."

    m "I-hrmm..."
    
    m "Inuendo aside, yes. He actually did. Which is why I know that he's not that kind of guy."

    n "A guy's a guy. 's all I'm sayin."

    "Natsuki shrugs and walks back towards her usual space near the closet. "

    "As she passes me and Sayori, she cuts her eyes towards me as she whispers with a sly smile."

    n "Keep your 'integrity' to yourself."

    "I turn about to retort, but realize it's a losing battle."

    m "Well, now that the trial of [player] v. Literature Club is over, time to get to the subject at hand; The festival. "

    m "There are a few more things I need to hammer out first, so for the time being, you all have some free time. "

    m "I encourage you to go over your poems and make sure you are proud of what you have. I will be printing them on pamphlets over the weekend, so I would like your written versions before we are dismissed. "

    m "We will also go over what we need over the weekend for Monday."

    "Everyone nods and heads over to their regular areas. "

    "As I think it over, I can just give her my poem now. "

    "I type it out on my phone to make sure I have a copy and send it to Monika. "

    "I hear her phone go off and she looks at it, and then back at me, before standing up and walking over."

    m "Hey."

    mc "H-hey."

    m "So, are you sure you want to do this one?"

    mc "Was it that ba-"

    "I stop myself as I notice the stern look on Monika's face."

    mc "Sorry. Force of habit. Yeah. I chose that one."

    m "I just want to be sure. The one you did yesterday was good too. It also feels like it's...how do I put this..."

    mc "Less bleak?"


    m "In...a way."

    mc "Hmm. I think that's why. I was thinking about what you said and, if I'm gonna give it my all, I need to do exactly that. "

    mc "I felt that this poem pulled out some of those emotions I just couldn't face for a while. But seeing it put into words helped. "

    mc "I just wanna see if it can help anyone else. I mean, that's how you triggered it out of me."

    m "I..what?"

    mc "The...song lyrics. I know it was just a mistake, but that was honestly a great motivation for me to actually self reflect. So, thank you."

    "Monika begins to turn red as she looks away smiling."

    m "Glad I was able to help. I just wanted to make sure you were going to be comfortable."

    m "I've spread the word myself, so I'm expecting somewhat of a crowd."

    mc "Sounds like a higher chance for potential members. Can't wait."

    "I smile at her and she lightly giggles back."

    m "Okay, I'll hold you to that."

    "Monika walks back to the teacher's desk. As I look around, I see Yuri and Natsuki are back where they usually are. "

    "Yuri seems calmer as she's already lost in her book. "

    "I turn to check what Natsuki is doing since I'm hearing faint chatter from there, and find her talking to Sayori."

    "They both look over towards me and stop talking. As we all stare at each other in an awkward silence, it is broken by Natsuki's outburst."

    n "Geez [player], get out of our business!"

    mc "Dah! I...I was just seeing if-"

    n "If you're that inclined to join in the girl talk, I can make you an honorary member."

    "I quickly turn around and face the front. I pull out my headphones and put them in and hit shuffle. "

    "As I listen to my music, I start thinking about the festival. "

    "Yeah, the performance is gonna suck, but once it's done, we should have the whole day ahead of us. "

    "This will be my first festival single. I might just see what the others are gonna do. "

    "That or just head home after hitting up a food stand or two."

    "As I think about the performance, I begin to remember about Yuri and how she was able to memorize her poem so quickly."

    "I try to do the same by closing my eyes and going over it in my head."

    "As I'm doing so, I then begin to imagine the performance. I can see myself standing at the front of the clubroom and the seats are filled with faceless people. "

    "As I keep going over my poem, the classroom begins to fill up and now there are people standing in the back. "

